# v1.5 layout swap: marketplace moved to / (index.html), editor moved to /build.html.
# Legacy marketplace URL → new root (Netlify preserves query strings on redirects).
/browse.html             /                            301
# Legacy editor recovery links (index.html?edit=<slug>) → the editor's new home.
# Netlify normalizes /index.html to / at the edge before rules run, so the
# root-path rule is the one that fires in production; the /index.html twin is
# kept for safety. Query-param rules match ONLY when ?edit= is the sole param
# (Netlify semantics) — anything else falls through to the marketplace file,
# whose client-side guard redirects the same way (covers local hosts too).
/            edit=:edit   /build.html?edit=:edit       301
/index.html  edit=:edit   /build.html?edit=:edit       301
